#: ../fhir-harness/processes/tools/ig-docs-site-compose.bpmn:14
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How a host docs site builds every IG it mounts INSIDE itself, so each IG's pages wear the host's chrome (one sidebar, one search, one language selector) rather than being a site of their own. Subprocess of Tool `stage-ig-sites`; reached from `docs-site-publish`'s `Call_InstanceSites` (skill `docs-generation`). NO IG PUBLISHER RUNS. `build-ig-site` turns the IG's source into Jekyll source, with the Publisher's `site.data.fhir` filled from the IG's AST and `sushi-config.yaml`, and the host's ONE Jekyll build renders it with just-the-docs (skill `ig-render-jekyll`). Which IGs is DATA: each instance whose `fhir-artifact-index/menu.json` records a `source.of` (the IG repository) and `source.ref` (the commit). No workflow and no step here names an IG. `feature-staging.yml` runs the same steps for a pull request's preview, with `--changed-files`, so only the IGs a change reaches are rebuilt. An IG repository building its OWN site runs `stage-ig-sites --only <instance> --source <checkout> --compose-into <shell> --compose-at-root`, which is `ig-ast-cache`'s `Task_BuildSite`, not this process."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/tools/ig-docs-site-compose.bpmn:73
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The host builds its Jekyll source ONCE (`bundle exec jekyll build --source ./_docs --destination ./_site`, Jekyll 4 with `jekyll-remote-theme` loading just-the-docs), then, for each line of the build list, runs Tool `build-ig-site` with `--dedupe-ids ./_site/<instance>`: it keeps the first copy of each anchor the IG's source repeats, renames the rest, and reports each one."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/tools/ig-docs-site-compose.bpmn:36
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The host has composed its docs layers into one Jekyll source (`compose-docs --out ./_docs`) and the IG instances are on disk: the remote mounts are replayed from the mount lock (e.g. `.github/mount-from-lock.sh`); `bun run cat state:mount` mounts state-branch graphs such as the work plan."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/tools/ig-docs-site-compose.bpmn:25
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The host's publish or preview job: GitHub Actions running each Tool's command in one runner. An instance with no recorded source is skipped and named, never silently absent, and a theme it cannot choose between is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/tools/ig-docs-site-compose.bpmn:40
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `ig-index-build`: `bun run cat ig-index:build`. Restores each IG's AST from its cache branch and writes `fhir-artifact-index/` (`index.json`, `menu.json` with the `source.of`/`source.ref` that `Task_Stage` clones from, `releases.json`, `package.tgz`). A missing input skips that instance, named."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/tools/ig-docs-site-compose.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `ig-pages`: `bun run fhir-harness/scripts/gen-ig-pages.ts --instance <instance> ...`, run for every IG instance by its own pages script. Writes `<instance>/docs/` from the artefact index: one thin page per artefact with its JSON-LD node, and, for an instance whose docs declare `igSite`, only a front-matter `artifacts.md`. Built at publish, never committed."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/tools/ig-docs-site-compose.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `stage-ig-sites` with `--compose-into ./_docs` (the same run as `Task_Stage`). Moves each staged site INTO the host's Jekyll source at `<instance>/`, with its includes and data namespaced per IG. Pages wear the thin layout with the host's chrome linked (`--full-pages` inlines the host's full chrome instead). Prints one `<instance> <jekyll source> <at>` line per IG: the build list the host keeps (`./_ig-list.txt`) for the post-build pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/tools/ig-docs-site-compose.bpmn:56
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `stage-ig-sites`: `bun run fhir-harness/scripts/stage-ig-sites.ts --work ./_ig --baseurl /<repo> --plantuml-jar <jar>`. Clones each IG at its recorded commit and stages ONE just-the-docs Jekyll source per IG with Tool `build-ig-site` (pages, includes, images, PlantUML, `_data/`, theme colours); the artefact lists (`artifacts`, `toc`) are thin pages over the artefact index node (Liquid only under `--full-pages`), and the instance's artefact pages from `Task_Pages` are copied in. The theme is the one `webpage` theme the instance declares or inherits along `needs`; two at the same distance are refused."
msgstr ""
